#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polynomial_expression_q

#% text
# `polynomial_expression_q(e, x)` gives true when e is a polynomial expression in x: built from x and expressions free of x by sums, products and non-negative integer powers.

#% text
# `polynomial_expression_q(e, [x1, ...])` uses several variables; `polynomial_expression_q(e, xs, test)` also requires every coefficient expression to pass test.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The expression is not expanded: `(x - 1)*(x - 2)^2` qualifies as it stands. A variable may be any expression, such as `sin(x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polynomial_expression_q(x^3 - a*x + (3*x - 1)^3*(x^4 + 1), x)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
polynomial_expression_q(x - 1/x, x)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
polynomial_expression_q(x^2*(y - x^3) + sin(z)*x*y, [x, y])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
polynomial_expression_q((x^2 - a*x*y + y)*(b*x + 4*x*y)^2, [x, y], is_numeric)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `variables`, `exponent`, `free_of`
